Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||10-30-2001||09:51 PM||||i took one out for a test drive last saturday.<BR>i cannot understand why the press likes this car so much. i was not at all impressed with the powertrain. it was very comfy (big hairy deal in my book), handles quite nice for an AWD, but the powertrain sucked. there was WAY too much turbo lag between shifts, and in general (&lt;4000rpm) and it was impossible to shift fast and smooth. i had to wait about 3 seconds between shifts for it to come back on smoothly. granted, i'd take a wagon if i ever had kids, but i dno't think it's as great a car as the critics say it is. or maybe they've just never driven a fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>anyone else driven one that would care to comment?||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||10-30-2001||10:00 PM||||...you need to learn how to shift.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Nah, I liked it, but it was part of the reason I'm getting the Fiero (finally). I got all hot and botheed about AWD till I ran the dogsnot out of one and realized it still didn't <I>rotate</I> around corners like a MR car can. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||10-30-2001||10:41 PM||||Didn't have a single problem. Subaru rocks. I've ALWAYS liked those cars. My fave was the SVX... Only flaw was that it was too heavy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||10-31-2001||01:29 AM||||I put one through it's pases (I LOVE it when the salesdroids decide they don't need to come with me, would YOU trust this man with your car?!?!<P>Anyway, I liked the car allright, but yes, of COURSE it has nothing below 4grand.  You have to *drive* the thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>PS: it seems to actually have a rearward torque bias, and that's all I am going to say.  I will not say how I was able to actually slide it around turns (raining) like a 'normal' car, just moreso.<P>Nice little car, launches like nothing you've ever seen....<BR>But I'm keeping my fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||filthyscarecrow||10-31-2001||01:43 AM||||i wonder if there was something wrong with the one i drive...<BR>the turbo lag between shifts was atrocious. (and just in case anyone doubts my ability to shift, i ~do~ have a racing license, hehe...) the other thing that i noticed is that the gearbox sucked. 1st through 4th were fairly close, but there was about a 2500RPM gap to 5th gear. it was like a 4spd with an overdrive. <BR>it handled quite nice, but it was offset by the poor power delivery. it also didn't seem that fast (i was shifting at redline, so i was driving it. the salesman told me to slow down plenty of times...). my integra felt faster, smoother, and easier to drive. i'm looking to drive an RSX type S. my friend ryan drove one in madison and he said ti kicked arse... i'm still baffled as to why the press likes the WRX so much though...||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||10-31-2001||03:37 AM||||The new WRXs do suck I heard. Besides the new horrible look they do not handle as well or go as well as the past models. I used to have a 1998 rex and it was one hot little machine.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||AutoXdbdragSE||10-31-2001||11:38 PM||||Just because you have a racing liscence doesn't mean your god. seriously though, how hard is one of those to get.. does it actualy mean anything or does it just mean you are resonably competent, and paid money?(not a make fun of type thing, earlier coment joke, this actually question)  the secret is rev the piss out of it, and once your foot touches the floor don't lift it. that's what they make revlimiters for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||11-01-2001||08:53 AM||||don't lift your foot on a shift if its a test drive....... howd you get a racing license and not know that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I think I'll go test drive one today and get back to you on that, I got a focus smoking pretty good last time.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||11-01-2001||09:50 AM||||Shifter was Rubbery<BR>Felt heavy and clumsy.<P><BR>Go drive a protege 5 (the little wagoon) not nearly as fast , but shifts so much nicer , better build quality and handles a lot better. My Girlfriend is looking at one.<P>I would sooner go buy a Used audi a4 than the wrx.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000009||avengador1||11-01-2001||05:56 PM||||I tried both the auto and the manual. The manual shifter didnt feel all that good. The car was very quick in both versions. Im thinking of getting one because of the awd and because weve been getting a lot of snow the past couple of years. I hate getting stuck in my own driveway with fwd Acura CL 3.0 while my wife's Subaru Legacy acts like the snow isn't even there.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
